    "evidence_text": "We build a dataset of 12,594 hashtags split into individual segments and propose a set of approaches for hashtag segmentation by framing it as a pairwise ranking problem between candidate segmentations.\n\nSegmentation as Pairwise Ranking\tThe goal of hashtag segmentation is to divide a given hashtag INLINEFORM0 into a sequence of meaningful words INLINEFORM1 .\n\nExperiments\tIn this section, we present experimental results that compare our proposed method with the other state-of-the-art approaches on hashtag segmentation datasets.\n\nThe next section will show experiments of applying hashtag segmentation to the popular task of sentiment analysis.\n\nWhile our hashtag segmentation model is achieving a very high accuracy@2, to be practically useful, it remains a challenge to get the top one predication exactly correct.\n\nOur hashtag segmenter successfully improved the sentiment analysis performance by 2% on average recall and F INLINEFORM0 comparing to having hashtags unsegmented.\n\nOther Related Work\tAutomatic hashtag segmentation can improve the performance of many applications besides sentiment analysis, such as text classification  , named entity linking  and modeling user interests for recommendations  .\n\nConclusion\tWe proposed a new pairwise neural ranking model for hashtag segmention and showed significant performance improvements over the state-of-the-art.\n\nWe demonstrated that hashtag segmentation helps with downstream tasks such as sentiment analysis.",
